# accounts spec criterion 2: doctor output from stubbed responses mirrors the real-world check in
# the spec: LOCAL Resource Explorer indexes in four regions and no aggregator, 649 supported types,
# and the Control Tower recorder (CONTINUOUS, allSupported) in eu-west-1 and eu-central-1 only.
env TEST_NOW=2026-11-10T12:00:00Z
env TEST_CASSETTE=$CASSETTES/aws/doctor-nonprod
exec tfcensus doctor --profile acme-nonprod
cmp stdout want-doctor.txt
! stderr .

# Within 24 hours the probe answers from the cache. Only the identity lookup calls AWS.
exec tfcensus doctor --profile acme-nonprod --format json
jsonschema report-v1.json stdout
stdout '"cached": true'
stdout '"supported_types": 649'
! stdout '"cached": false'
exists .cache/tfcensus/probe/111111111111/account.json
exists .cache/tfcensus/probe/111111111111/us-east-1.json

# --refresh probes again.
exec tfcensus doctor --profile acme-nonprod --format md --refresh
cmp stdout want-doctor.md

-- home/.aws/config --
[profile acme-nonprod]
region = eu-west-1
aws_access_key_id = AKIAFAKE
aws_secret_access_key = fake-secret
-- want-doctor.txt --
SOURCE        KIND     ACCOUNT       NAME          STATUS
acme-nonprod  profile  111111111111  acme-nonprod  ok

ACCOUNT       REGION        RESOURCE EXPLORER    CONFIG                                 AGGREGATORS  LAYERS
111111111111  eu-central-1  local, default view  recording (continuous, all supported)  none         re, config, cc, native
111111111111  eu-north-1    local, no view       no recorder                            none         cc, native
111111111111  eu-west-1     local, default view  recording (continuous, all supported)  none         re, config, cc, native
111111111111  us-east-1     local, default view  no recorder                            none         re, cc, native

111111111111 (acme-nonprod): Resource Explorer supports 649 resource types.
111111111111 (acme-nonprod): Resource Explorer has local indexes only, so tfcensus searches each region on its own. An admin can promote one to an aggregator (`aws resource-explorer-2 update-index-type --type AGGREGATOR`).
111111111111 (acme-nonprod): eu-north-1: the Resource Explorer index has no view, and tfcensus never creates one. An admin can create a default view (`aws resource-explorer-2 create-view`, then `associate-default-view`).
111111111111 (acme-nonprod): eu-north-1: no AWS Config recorder, so the config layer is off here.
111111111111 (acme-nonprod): us-east-1: no AWS Config recorder, so the config layer is off here.
-- want-doctor.md --
| SOURCE | KIND | ACCOUNT | NAME | STATUS |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| acme-nonprod | profile | 111111111111 | acme-nonprod | ok |

| ACCOUNT | REGION | RESOURCE EXPLORER | CONFIG | AGGREGATORS | LAYERS |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 111111111111 | eu-central-1 | local, default view | recording (continuous, all supported) | none | re, config, cc, native |
| 111111111111 | eu-north-1 | local, no view | no recorder | none | cc, native |
| 111111111111 | eu-west-1 | local, default view | recording (continuous, all supported) | none | re, config, cc, native |
| 111111111111 | us-east-1 | local, default view | no recorder | none | re, cc, native |

## 111111111111 (acme-nonprod)

- Resource Explorer supports 649 resource types.
- Resource Explorer has local indexes only, so tfcensus searches each region on its own. An admin can promote one to an aggregator (`aws resource-explorer-2 update-index-type --type AGGREGATOR`).
- eu-north-1: the Resource Explorer index has no view, and tfcensus never creates one. An admin can create a default view (`aws resource-explorer-2 create-view`, then `associate-default-view`).
- eu-north-1: no AWS Config recorder, so the config layer is off here.
- us-east-1: no AWS Config recorder, so the config layer is off here.
